\subsection{Hard-iron correction result}
\label{sec:mag-hi-results}

The hard-iron correction is evaluated under the deterministic protocol: one
realization per stationary record, the default sensor-error draw, and the final
\SI{900}{s}.  Enabling it reduces yaw RMS on all eight records; the mean falls
from \SI{1.835}{\degree} to \SI{0.822}{\degree} and the worst case from
\SI{2.162}{\degree} to \SI{1.063}{\degree}.  Pitch changes slightly, while roll
and displacement are negligible.  Because matched OU--II uses the same magnetic
correction, this effect does not contribute to the reported
OU--III-minus-OU--II translational difference.

\begin{table}[t]
  \centering
  \caption{Hard-iron correction effect on attitude RMS.}
  \label{tab:mag-hi-yaw}
  \setlength{\tabcolsep}{4pt}
  \renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.08}
  \footnotesize
  \sisetup{detect-all}
  \begin{tabular}{@{}l
                  S[table-format=1.2]
                  S[table-format=1.3]
                  S[table-format=1.3]
                  S[table-format=1.3]
                  S[table-format=1.3]
                  @{}}
    \toprule
    {Case} & {$H_s$} & \multicolumn{2}{c}{Yaw RMS (\si{\degree})}
           & \multicolumn{2}{c}{Pitch RMS (\si{\degree})} \\
    \cmidrule(lr){3-4}\cmidrule(lr){5-6}
    {} & {\si{m}} & {off} & {on} & {off} & {on} \\
    \midrule
    JONSWAP    & 0.27 & 2.075 & 1.063 & 0.174 & 0.175 \\
    JONSWAP    & 1.50 & 1.825 & 1.050 & 0.169 & 0.152 \\
    JONSWAP    & 4.00 & 1.298 & 1.041 & 0.358 & 0.330 \\
    JONSWAP    & 8.50 & 1.104 & 0.709 & 0.469 & 0.445 \\
    \addlinespace
    PM--Stokes & 0.27 & 2.155 & 0.741 & 0.200 & 0.200 \\
    PM--Stokes & 1.50 & 2.162 & 1.026 & 0.223 & 0.208 \\
    PM--Stokes & 4.00 & 2.053 & 0.473 & 0.278 & 0.235 \\
    PM--Stokes & 8.50 & 2.007 & 0.476 & 0.259 & 0.196 \\
    \midrule
    {mean}     & {}   & 1.835 & 0.822 & 0.266 & 0.243 \\
    {worst}    & {}   & 2.162 & 1.063 & 0.469 & 0.445 \\
    \bottomrule
  \end{tabular}
\end{table}

This result is conditional on the reported calibration draw.  Additional
misalignment-dominated draws can regress because soft-iron and misalignment
terms alias into the additive fit while satisfying its residual gate.  The
correction is therefore not claimed as a complete magnetometer calibration;
full distortion identification requires multi-heading excitation.

\subsection{Embedded portability}
\label{sec:real-hardware-platform}

The same estimator source compiles and executes on an M5Stack AtomS3R
(ESP32--S3) with calibrated MEMS input (Fig.~\ref{fig:atoms3r-platform}).

\begin{figure}[!t]
  \centering
  \includesvg[width=0.25\columnwidth,inkscapelatex=false]{AtomS3R_device}
  \caption{M5Stack AtomS3R embedded validation target.}
  \label{fig:atoms3r-platform}
\end{figure}

This establishes functional source portability only.  Processor load, memory,
power, deadline margin, thermal behavior, and externally referenced
reconstruction accuracy were not measured.
